---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head><BaseHead title="About" description="Meet F1 bits: independent Formula 1 commentary, our sourcing standards, and our corrections policy." /></head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main id="main" tabindex="-1">
			<p class="eyebrow">About the publication</p>
			<h1>A closer look at the fastest sport.</h1>
			<p class="intro">F1 bits follows the people, decisions, and places behind Formula 1. Driver-market intrigue. The thinking behind a race. What a new circuit means beyond its launch announcement.</p>
			<h2>Independent, by design</h2>
			<p>This is an independent editorial project maintained by <a href="https://github.com/RobertBord">RobertBord</a>. We are not affiliated with Formula 1, the FIA, any team, or any driver, and do not claim paddock access or inside sources.</p>
			<h2 id="standards">Editorial standards</h2>
			<p>Confirmed facts come from identifiable sources, with preference for official announcements, regulations, and on-record statements. We link the evidence so readers can inspect it.</p>
			<p>Reported rumours are labelled and attributed. A driver being eligible for a seat does not mean a team is negotiating with them. Analysis is our interpretation of the evidence, not a claim of inside knowledge.</p>
			<p>Time-sensitive stories carry a reporting cutoff. Historical analysis stays anchored to that date rather than quietly presenting old predictions as current news. We do not manufacture quotes or use speculative headlines as statements of fact.</p>
			<h2>Corrections &amp; contact</h2>
			<p>Found an error? <a href="https://github.com/RobertBord/cs4421-astro-blog/issues/new?labels=content&amp;title=Editorial%20correction">Raise an editorial correction</a> with the article URL, the disputed claim, and a supporting source. Do not include private personal information. Substantive corrections will be noted in the article with an updated date.</p>
			<h2>Images &amp; attribution</h2>
			<p>Photography and illustrations are credited alongside the work. Illustrations are not evidence of an event or a representation of an announced circuit design. Third-party trademarks belong to their respective owners.</p>
			<a href="/blog/">Read the latest articles</a>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
<style>
	h1 { font-size: 3rem; }
	h2 { font-size: 1.75rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; }
	.intro { font-size: 1.2rem; color: rgb(var(--gray)); }
	@media (max-width: 680px) { h1 { font-size: 2.25rem; } }
</style>